  "question": {
    "text": "If the tangents drawn at the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;on the circle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;intersect at the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math>, then the area of the triangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math> is equal to"
  },
